# Comparisons of the thread index with the CTA index, per CTA. With no
# grid each is an unknown selector. With one, a lane is in at every CTA,
# at none, or at some, and the per-CTA counts are bounds: the lanes in at
# some CTA, `<=`. A comparison the grid decides folds, and one whose
# %ctaid terms take one value loses them.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/cta_guards.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=FREE "%s"
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/cta_guards.ptx --grid 2 | FileCheck --check-prefix=TWO "%s"
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/cta_guards.ptx --grid 8 | FileCheck --check-prefix=EIGHT "%s"

FREE: kernel micro_cta_compare
FREE: st.global.u32  global store 4 B (predicated)
FREE: totals per CTA [static]:
FREE: global bytes: load 0 B, store <= 768 B
FREE: kernel micro_cta_branch
FREE: st.global.u32  global store 4 B on <= 16 threads in <= 1 warps (%tid.x < 16)
FREE: st.global.u32  global store 4 B on <= 32 threads in <= 1 warps ((%tid.x < 16 or ?))
FREE: totals per CTA [static]:
FREE: global bytes: load 0 B, store <= 448 B
FREE: kernel micro_cta_rows
FREE: st.global.u32  global store 4 B (predicated)

# Under 2 CTAs, t < 2c holds at some CTA on lanes 0 and 1, t <= 2c on
# lane 0 at every CTA and on lanes 1 and 2 at some; the six total
# 4·(2 + 3 + 31 + 32 + 3 + 32) = 412 B. %ctaid.x < 2 holds and
# %ctaid.x >= 4 does not, so the branch kernel is exact.
TWO: kernel micro_cta_compare
TWO: st.global.u32  global store 4 B on <= 2 threads in <= 1 warps (%tid.x - 2 * %ctaid.x < 0)
TWO: st.global.u32  global store 4 B on <= 3 threads in 1 warp (%tid.x - 2 * %ctaid.x <= 0)
TWO: st.global.u32  global store 4 B on <= 31 threads in 1 warp (%tid.x - 2 * %ctaid.x > 0)
TWO: st.global.u32  global store 4 B on <= 32 threads in 1 warp (%tid.x - 2 * %ctaid.x >= 0)
TWO: st.global.u32  global store 4 B on <= 3 threads in <= 1 warps (%tid.x - 2 * %ctaid.x == 0)
TWO: st.global.u32  global store 4 B on <= 32 threads in 1 warp (%tid.x - 2 * %ctaid.x != 0)
TWO: totals per CTA [static]:
TWO: global bytes: load 0 B, store <= 412 B
TWO: kernel micro_cta_branch
TWO: st.global.u32  global store 4 B on 16 threads in 1 warp (%tid.x < 16)
TWO: st.global.u32  global store 4 B (predicated)
TWO: st.global.u32  global store 4 B on 16 threads in 1 warp (%tid.x >= 16)
TWO: totals per CTA [static]:
TWO: global bytes: load 0 B, store 384 B
# A block of 40×2: x + 16·c < 24 holds on x < 8 at both CTAs, on
# x < 24 at CTA 0, two rows each; the third warp's 16 lanes are x >= 24.
TWO: kernel micro_cta_rows
TWO: st.global.u32  global store 4 B on <= 48 threads in 2 warps (%tid.x + 16 * %ctaid.x < 24)
TWO: totals per CTA [static]:
TWO: global bytes: load 0 B, store <= 192 B

# Under 8 CTAs %ctaid.x < 4 selects the block on some CTAs only.
EIGHT: kernel micro_cta_branch
EIGHT: <block 1>  (no line info)      10  <= 32 in <= 1 warps (%ctaid.x < 4)
EIGHT: st.global.u32  global store 4 B on <= 16 threads in <= 1 warps (%ctaid.x < 4 and %tid.x < 16 and %ctaid.x < 2)
EIGHT: totals per CTA [static]:
EIGHT: global bytes: load 0 B, store <= 448 B
